All checks are complete. Here's the summary:

## Screens covered

The app is a two-screen resume builder (Dashboard ↔ Editor, switched in `Index.tsx`) plus a 404 route:

- **Dashboard** (`src/components/dashboard/Dashboard.tsx`, `ResumeCard.tsx`) — new-resume action, search input, sort select, empty-state action, and the resumes grid as a folded collection (each card's menu, rename dialog, delete dialog all hinted).
- **Editor** (`src/components/editor/ResumeEditor.tsx` + 7 form components + `TemplateSelector`/`SectionManager`) — back navigation, title edit, preview toggle, the 7-tab bar folded as a collection with per-tab regions, and every form field across Contact/Summary/Experience/Education/Skills/Template/Sections.
- **Live Preview** (`ModernTemplate.tsx`, `ClassicTemplate.tsx`, `MinimalTemplate.tsx`) — observable mirrors of the same resume data, so an agent can verify edits actually rendered.
- **404 page** (`NotFound.tsx`) — the "Return to Home" link.

## Id namespaces

`dashboard.*` (search, sort, newResume, resumes.grid.item.<resumeId>.*), `editor.*` (back, title, previewToggle, tabs.item.<tabId>, contact/summary/experience/education/skills/template/sections.*, preview.*), `notFound.home`. State keys use domain names (`contact.fullName`, `experience.company`, `resume.title`, `skill.name`, etc.) shared between the editing control and its display in the live preview, per §5 of the spec.

## Collections folded (§7)

Resume grid, editor tabs, experience list, education list, skills list, template options, section-order list, and (in each preview template) experience/education/skills lists — all keyed by stable ids (`resume.id`, `exp.id`, `edu.id`, `skill.id`, `tab.id`, `section.id`), never array index.

## Collection I could not fully fold

`ClassicTemplate`'s skills section renders `resume.skills.map(s => s.name).join(' • ')` as one flattened string with no per-item DOM nodes, so it only gets a single aggregate `observable` (`editor.preview.skills.text`) instead of per-item folding — Modern/Minimal do fold it since they render one `<span>` per skill.

## Deliberately left unhinted

- `src/components/NavLink.tsx` — a generic wrapper component that's never actually used anywhere in the app.
- Decorative icons, layout wrappers, and the "Live Preview" section label.
- Shared shadcn/ui primitives needed no prop-widening — `Button`, `Input`, `Textarea`, `Checkbox`, `Switch`, `Select`/`Tabs`/`Dialog`/`DropdownMenu` parts already spread `{...props}` onto their DOM root, so `data-semtag-*` passes through as-is.

## Validation & checks

- `validate-semtags.mjs src` → **0 errors**, 131 hinted elements, 10 warnings — all 10 are `duplicate-id` on the three preview templates, which is a static-analysis false positive: I confirmed in `ResumePreview.tsx` that Modern/Classic/Minimal are rendered via a mutually-exclusive `switch`, so only one is ever mounted at a time and the shared ids never collide at runtime.
- `tsc --noEmit`, `npm run build` → clean (pre-existing CSS `@import`-order warning, unrelated).
- `npm run lint` → 4 pre-existing errors (in `Dashboard.tsx`'s `let filtered`, `command.tsx`, `textarea.tsx`, `tailwind.config.ts`) — I verified via `git diff` that none of these lines were touched by my edits; they predate this work.

